\f0\fs30 \cf0 #About Extensiv Design Kit\
Extensiv Design Kit is based on MUI design system with custom styles. It also has a small number of custom components that will be added to this design system later. \
\
\'97\
\
#Colors\
The Primary colour palette is based on Extensiv brand colours Teal/Dark Teal. It is used for UI elements like Primary buttons, switches, radio and checkboxes, etc.\
Other brand / marketing colors (Plum, Berry, Magenta, Energy Orange, Yellow/Sunflower) are used primarily in marketing materials. Do not use in the product UI unless explicitly instructed.\
\
\'97\
\
#Icons\
\
##Font Awesome\
\
Font Awesome is our default icon set. It is mostly used for illustrative purposes. \
\
Our preferred icon style is sharp-solid. To improve the recognition of the icon (for example, cloud, gear, etc.), other styles can be used: sharp-regular, solid, regular.\
\
The best Scale options are: \
- .75x  |  (15 x 15 px, including padding)\
- 1x    |  (20 x 20 px, including padding)\
- 1.25x |  (25 x 25 px, including padding)\
\
Double check icon names before using them to avoid hallucinations. \
\
##Material icons\
\
The original Material icons are still used as integral parts of certain components (such as Checkbox, Radio, Select, etc.) They mostly serve functional rather than illustrative purposes.\
\
\'97\
\
#Components\
\
The Figma file lists multiple components. To begin with, we can only include the key components in this design system, and add others later. \
\
##Key components\
\
###INPUTS\
\
####Button \
Use `contained` variant with `primary` color as the main CTA. Limit to one instance per view.\
Use `outlined` variant with `inherit` color for all other CTAs.\
The colors `error` and `warning` can be used when the button is a part of another component (e.g. Alert), as defined by the design system Figma file. Don\'92t use them outside of these components unless explicitly asked.\
\
